Title: "Label Headers"
Id: "ef950516-d94c-451b-ac4b-d4075dbfe434"

Text: "Label headers are bracketed names used for theorem-like labels and optional nested labels.

```mlg-fragment
[theorem.ordinal.trichotomy]
Theorem:
then: ...

[case.left]
allOf:
. P
. Q
```

Dotted labels are useful because renderers can turn dots into spaces for fallback titles, while source stays precise. Unlike expression labels (`[:a.b:]`), a label header may contain stropped symbolic name parts.

A label heading is optional on alias items, `Requires:`/`Enables:` items, documented items, specify items, and clause groups. It is **required** on the `have:`/`asserting:` items of a `Justification:` section, where it pairs with a `[:label:]` on a formulation elsewhere in the same group."
Id: "88b282a9-4078-4473-acb4-ebbe5ed34d0f"
